{
 "name": "Risk of Rain 2",
 "name_ko": "리스크 오브 레인 2",
 "exe": "Risk of Rain 2.exe",
 "engine": "wwise",
 "event_file": "C:\\Users\\Public\\dshaptics\\events_unity.log",
 "_run_note": "Unity + Wwise. Hook = BepInEx 5 + SonmatUnity.dll (part sonmat-unity): every sound by name, with its owner (GameObject). Sounds = the game's own Wwise banks (unity_wwise reader, as autosetup). The DualSense reaches the game through Steam Input / XInput; the game's own vibration (screen shake, RoR2.dll DefaultGamepadVibrationController) is cut by sonmat_rumble.dll when the switch is off.",
 "_controls_note": "Pad layout = the usual default (not readable from this install: no Rewired InputManager in level0; from general knowledge): R2 = primary skill (held = auto-fire), L2 = secondary, L1 = utility, R1 = special, A/cross = jump, Y/triangle = interact, X/square = equipment. One mode: third-person shooter, 17+ survivors, each with m1/m2/shift/R (or skill1..4) sounds named after it. The biggest moments: the boss spawning (Play_boss_spawn_rumble), the teleporter finishing (Play_UI_teleporter_event_complete), a boss dying, my death, the drop pod landing at the start of a stage.",
 "_places_note": "Stages are open maps (plains, desert, snow, lakes, caves, the moon); no vehicles, no water you swim in. Geysers launch you (Play_env_geyser_launch). No floor switch: one footstep name for every ground.",
 "_owner_note": "Owners: my body plays Play_Player_footstep, my jumps and landings; my shots and their hits are played by the projectiles (a new GameObject each) - so shots go by the survivor's name (only my survivor's names come in solo), not by owner. Play_UI_hit / Play_UI_crit = MY damage landing (a hit marker, UI object), Play_UI_takeDamage = I am hurt. <monster>_impact = that monster being hit (by me or my drones): not used, UI_hit says it once.",
 "player": "^Play_Player_footstep$",
